Hyprlume is available under MIT OR Apache-2.0.

Hyprlume uses hyprpilot-core from HyprPilot (MIT OR Apache-2.0):
https://github.com/sumerchoudhary78/HyprPilot

Local speech inference uses sherpa-onnx (Apache-2.0) and ONNX Runtime (MIT):
https://github.com/k2-fsa/sherpa-onnx
https://github.com/microsoft/onnxruntime

Quickshell/Qt and espeak-ng are separately installed programs. Their licenses
apply to those programs. Hyprlume does not link espeak-ng or piper-phonemize.

Speech weights are not included in this repository or package. The opt-in
model installer downloads upstream archives, verifies pinned SHA-256 digests,
and retains upstream model cards and attribution. Model licenses remain
independent of Hyprlume's source license.

Desktop visual assets
---------------------
The observatory backdrop and transparent assistant are generated project assets.
Prompts and origins are documented in shell/assets/README.md and docs/design/.
The globe uses public-domain Natural Earth land geometry. No third-party 3D
model pack is bundled. Qt Quick 3D and other runtime packages retain their own
licenses and are installed separately.
